nstruction, even though the\\nzero-wait data memory returns the load word combinationally in MEM. CoreMark has\\nmany pointer-chasing and structure-access sequences where a load is consumed\\nimmediately, so this conservative interlock directly reduces iterations per\\ncycle; random dmem backpressure already provides the hold mechanism needed when\\nthe returned word is not yet valid.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a true MEM-to-EX result bypass that forwards the extracted and extended load\\nvalue, rather than the EX/MEM address, to the following instruction. Remove the\\nunconditional load-use bubble: if dmem is ready, the dependent instruction can\\nexecute in the same cycle that the load occupies MEM; if dmem is stalled, retain\\nboth the load and its consumer and suppress redirects until the valid load value\\narrives. This structural forwarding path should improve CoreMark IPC enough to\\noutweigh its modest added load-data-to-ALU timing cone, while preserving in-order\\nretirement, exactly-once memory effects, RVFI operand values, and the nret=1\\ninterface.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the current MEM-stage architectural result, selecting the sign/zero-extended load value for loads and the registered ALU result otherwise, as an EX forwarding source.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat an EX/MEM load as forwardable from the new MEM result path while retaining youngest-writer priority and x0 suppression.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the MEM-stage result bypass and suppress dependent branch or jump redirects while an older memory transaction is held by dmem backpressure.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the fixed load-use bubble and rely on the existing whole-pipeline dmem hold when a forwarded load result is not ready.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/zcore.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the MEM-stage load result into the EX forwarding input and preserve the existing bus-stall and nret=1 RVFI topology.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed load-to-ALU, load-to-store, and load-to-branch dependency tests with zero-wait and randomized multi-cycle dmem stalls, checking no bubble in the ready case and exactly-once ordered RVFI retirement.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the current MEM-stage architectural result, selecting the sign/zero-extended load value for loads and the registered ALU result otherwise, as an EX forwarding source.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat an EX/MEM load as forwardable from the new MEM result path while retaining youngest-writer priority and x0 suppression.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the MEM-stage result bypass and suppress dependent branch or jump redirects while an older memory transaction is held by dmem backpressure.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the fixed load-use bubble and rely on the existing whole-pipeline dmem hold when a forwarded load result is not ready.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/zcore.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the MEM-stage load result into the EX forwarding input and preserve the existing bus-stall and nret=1 RVFI topology.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed load-to-ALU, load-to-store, and load-to-branch dependency tests with zero-wait and randomized multi-cycle dmem stalls, checking no bubble in the ready case and exactly-once ordered RVFI retirement.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: reg_ch0\\nshed (returncode=0)\\nSBY 17:52:21 [insn_sw_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\\nSBY 17:52:21 [insn_sw_ch0] 