hput, likely depressing FPGA\\nFmax in a core already using 9563 LUT4s.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The combinational ALU currently instantiates three independent 64-bit products for\\nsigned-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and signed-unsigned multiplication. Only one ALU\\noperation can execute per cycle, so the duplicated multiplier hardware adds DSP/LUT\\nusage and routing congestion without increasing throughput, likely depressing FPGA\\nFmax in a core already using 9563 LUT4s.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Compute one 32x32 unsigned 64-bit product and derive MULH and MULHSU high halves with\\ntwo's-complement sign-correction subtractors. MUL continues to select the shared\\nproduct's low half and MULHU its high half. Sharing the expensive product should\\nimprove placement and timing while preserving the existing single-cycle EX latency,\\ninstruction-per-cycle behavior, ALTOPS formal branch, and all RV32M edge semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the three parallel multiply expressions with one unsigned 32x32 product and sign-corrected high-half results for MULH and MULHSU.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed and randomized cross-sign multiply vectors that verify all four MUL-family results after multiplier sharing.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the three parallel multiply expressions with one unsigned 32x32 product and sign-corrected high-half results for MULH and MULHSU.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed and randomized cross-sign multiply vectors that verify all four MUL-family results after multiplier sharing.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"implementation_compile_failed: \", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 1}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Replace combinational division with an iterative M-unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The post-route critical path runs from ID/EX through the synthesized divide/remainder cone into EX/MEM, reaching roughly 7.9 ns and limiting the median Fmax to 127.03 MHz. The same combinational divider also contributes substantial LUT and routing pressure in a design already using 9563 LUT4s, whereas the CoreMark binary contains only a handful of static DIVU sites.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The post-route critical path runs from ID/EX through the synthesized divide/remainder cone into EX/MEM, reaching roughly 7.9 ns and limiting the median Fmax to 127.03 MHz. The same combinational divider also contributes substantial LUT and routing pressure in a design already using 9563 LUT4s, whereas the CoreMark binary contains only a handful of static DIVU sites.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU out of the combinational ALU into a shared radix-2 iterative divider. On a divide instruction, capture the forwarded operands and instruction metadata, freeze the younger pipeline and EX/MEM advancement while the unit iterates, then inject the architecturally correct quotient or remainder into EX/MEM exactly once when done. Keep ordinary ALU and DSP-backed multiply instructions single-cycle. Removing the unrolled divider cone should materially raise Fmax and reduce placement congestion; the low dynamic division frequency should make the added divide latency much smaller than the clock-rate gain. Preserve divide-by-zero and signed-overflow semantics, RVFI operands/order, bus-stall priority, redirects, and the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 15, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/div_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a shared iterative signed/unsigned quotient-remainder unit with start, busy, done, and result handshaking plus all RV32M corner-case semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational divide and remainder operators from the normal hardware datapath while retaining the ALTOPS formal substitutions and single-cycle non-divide operations.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize divide-class operations, capture their forwarded operands and pipeline payload, wait for the iterative result, and emit one completed EX/MEM transaction without duplicate redirects or retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add multi-cycle execute interlocking that freezes IF and ID, prevents EX/MEM overwrite, and composes correctly with instruction/data bus stalls and redirect flushing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the divider busy/completion handshake through execute and hazard control while preserving the nret=1 top-level and RVFI interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Adapt unit coverage so combinational ALU tests continue to cover non-divide and ALTOPS behavior while division correctness is exercised through the multi-cycle path.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add pipeline tests for dependent and back-to-back DIV/REM operations, corner cases, random imem/dmem stalls, and exactly-once RVFI retirement during execute interlocks.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 15, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/div_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a shared iterative signed/unsigned quotient-remainder unit with start, busy, done, and result handshaking plus all RV32M corner-case semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational divide and remainder operators from the normal hardware datapath while retaining the ALTOPS formal substitutions and single-cycle non-divide operations.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize divide-class operations, capture their forwarded operands and pipeline payload, wait for the iterative result, and emit one completed EX/MEM transaction without duplicate redirects or retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add multi-cycle execute interlocking that freezes IF and ID, prevents EX/MEM overwrite, and composes correctly with instruction/data bus stalls and redirect flushing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the divider busy/completion handshake through execute and hazard control while preserving the nret=1 top-level and RVFI interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Adapt unit coverage so combinational ALU tests continue to cover non-divide and ALTOPS behavior while division correctness is exercised through the multi-cycle path.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add pipeline tests for dependent and back-to-back DIV/REM operations, corner cases, random imem/dmem stalls, and exactly-once RVFI retirement during execute interlocks.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 441.11, \"delta_pct\": 55.97, \"vs_baseline\": 55.97, \"fmax_mhz\": 198.14, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5376, \"ff\": 2085, \"seeds\": [198.14, 204.92, 197.36], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T20:45:07.936221Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-002-r1s1 (improvement, +55.97%): Replacing the combinational DIV/REM cone with a shared radix-2 iterative M-unit greatly improves Fmax and routing efficiency when CoreMark's low dynamic divide frequency amortizes the resulting pipeline freezes.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Fetch-time backward-branch and JAL prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current pipeline waits until EX to redirect every taken branch and jump,\\nflushing younger work even for regular loop backedges and direct calls. CoreMark\\ncontains frequent counted loops, so these repeated control penalties directly\\nreduce iterations per cycle under the benchmark's instruction-bus stalls.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current pipeline waits until EX to redirect every taken branch and jump,\\nflushing younger work even for regular loop backedges and direct calls. CoreMark\\ncontains frequent counted loops, so these repeated control penalties directly\\nreduce iterations per cycle under the benchmark's instruction-bus stalls.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a minimal static predictor in IF that always predicts direct JAL targets and\\npredicts conditional branches backward-taken, forward-not-taken. Carry the\\npredicted next PC with each instruction and make EX redirect and flush only when\\nthe resolved next PC differs from that prediction. This should eliminate most\\nloop-backedge and direct-jump bubbles with little state or LUT cost, preserving\\nFmax better than a tagged BTB or dynamic history table.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 9, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline payloads.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode fetch-time branch/JAL immediates, apply backward-taken and direct-JAL prediction, and emit the selected predicted next PC.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pipeline the fetch prediction metadata alongside the instruction into EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare resolved next PC with the carried prediction and request recovery only on a mismatch, while retaining architectural pc_wdata and trap behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Rename and connect the EX recovery signals through IF and hazard control as a misprediction redirect.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat the EX recovery indication as a misprediction flush so correctly predicted taken control flow is not squashed.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for correct backward-branch and JAL predictions, forward-branch fall-through, and taken/not-taken misprediction recovery.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 9, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline payloads.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode fetch-time branch/JAL immediates, apply backward-taken and direct-JAL prediction, and emit the selected predicted next PC.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pipeline the fetch prediction metadata alongside the instruction into EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare resolved next PC with the carried prediction and request recovery only on a mismatch, while retaining architectural pc_wdata and trap behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Rename and connect the EX recovery signals through IF and hazard control as a misprediction redirect.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat the EX recovery indication as a misprediction flush so correctly predicted taken control flow is not squashed.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for correct backward-branch and JAL predictions, forward-branch fall-through, and taken/not-taken misprediction recovery.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"implementation_compile_failed: \", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:5:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Qualify load-use hazards by source operands\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use detector compares a load destination against both raw rs1 and rs2\\nbit fields of every following instruction. Many RV32I formats do not consume one\\nor either of those fields, so immediate payload bits that happen to equal the load\\ndestination create unnecessary one-cycle bubbles in CoreMark's load-heavy code.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use detector compares a load destination against both raw rs1 and rs2\\nbit fields of every following instruction. Many RV32I formats do not consume one\\nor either of those fields, so immediate payload bits that happen to equal the load\\ndestination create unnecessary one-cycle bubbles in CoreMark's load-heavy code.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Decode whether the IF/ID instruction actually reads rs1 and rs2, and qualify each\\nload-use comparison with the corresponding source-use bit. Real load dependencies\\nwill retain their required bubble, while false matches in OP-IMM, LOAD, JALR,\\nLUI/AUIPC, JAL, FENCE, and SYSTEM instructions will flow without stalling. This\\nsmall opcode-only guard should improve iterations per cycle with negligible area\\nand timing cost, while leaving forwarding, bus backpressure, retirement, and all\\narchitectural behavior unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive RV32IM rs1/rs2 source-use qualifiers from the IF/ID opcode and gate load-use matches so only true dependencies stall.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/zcore.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the complete IF/ID instruction into the hazard unit while preserving the existing nret=1 top-level interface and stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks that true load consumers still bubble and false matches in unused instruction fields do not stall or alter RVFI retirement.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_