{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n \\\"hypothesis.schema|safe_load|jsonschema\\\" tools schemas Makefile | head -n 80 && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r9s0.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r9s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"tools/tournament.py:54:# The hypothesis schema's `category` enum, in the order the brief specifies.\ntools/tournament.py:218:    import jsonschema\ntools/tournament.py:262:    except (jsonschema.ValidationError, FileNotFoundError, yaml.YAMLError) as e:\ntools/agents/static_agent.py:94:        \"      No-op placeholder to satisfy the hypothesis schema's\\n\"\ntools/agents/implement.py:170:        hypothesis = yaml.safe_load(f)\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:161:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:185:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:218:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:235:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/eval/formal.py:32:    y = yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()) or {}\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:282:## Required YAML structure (validates against schemas/hypothesis.schema.json)\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:338:        data = yaml.safe_load(raw)\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:351:            data = yaml.safe_load(repaired)\ntools/test_core_yaml_update.py:24:    y = yaml.safe_load((core_dir / \"core.yaml\").read_text())\ntools/orchestrator.py:6:import jsonschema, yaml\ntools/orchestrator.py:48:HYP_SCHEMA     = json.loads(Path(\"schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\").read_text())\ntools/orchestrator.py:152:    y = yaml.safe_load(yaml_path.read_text()) or {}\ntools/orchestrator.py:365:                    y = yaml.safe_load(candidate.read_text()) or {}\ntools/orchestrator.py:446:        hyp = yaml.safe_load(f)\ntools/orchestrator.py:447:    jsonschema.validate(hyp, HYP_SCHEMA)\ntools/orchestrator.py:605:        y = yaml.safe_load((src / \"core.yaml\").read_text()) or {}\ntools/bench/runner.py:99:    cfg = yaml.safe_load(path.read_text())\nid: hyp-20260711-001-r9s0\ntitle: \"Canonical source-aware load interlock\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The load-use interlock still compares a pending load destination with both raw\n  register fields of the following instruction. Immediate bits and other unused\n  fields can therefore alias the load destination and insert unnecessary bubbles\n  in CoreMark. Earlier attempts showed that removing those bubbles is only safe\n  when hazard detection, forwarding, and RVFI all agree on which sources exist.\nhypothesis: |\n  Extend the existing decoder with rs1-used and rs2-used outputs, defaulting both\n  false and asserting them only in fully validated instruction arms. In ID, use\n  those bits to canonicalize every unused source address and value to zero before\n  the ID/EX register, and expose the same canonical combinational addresses to the\n  load-use detector. Thus false raw-field aliases no longer stall, while every\n  true dependency retains its bubble and forwarding behavior. Using one decoded\n  source definition for the interlock and retired RVFI metadata directly addresses\n  the prior reg_ch0 failure without adding a 32-bit mux or a new cross-stage path,\n  so CoreMark cycles should fall with little effect on the current high Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n    description: \"Add default-false rs1-used and rs2-used outputs and assert them only for validated encodings that architecturally consume each source.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Canonicalize unused source addresses and values to zero, using the same decode outputs for regfile reads, ID/EX forwarding metadata, and downstream RVFI.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Consume canonical IF/ID source addresses so load-use detection stalls only for true architectural dependencies.\"\n  - file: rtl/zcore.sv\n    description: \"Wire ID's canonical combinational source addresses into the hazard unit while preserving all existing bus-stall priorities and the nret=1 interface.\"\n  - file: test/test_decoder.py\n    description: \"Verify source-use metadata for every legal instruction class plus reserved and illegal encodings.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check true load dependencies, false aliases in unused fields, canonical RVFI source metadata, and behavior under randomized imem and dmem stalls.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
