{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r12s1.yaml; rg -n 'hypothesis.schema|jsonschema|safe_load' tools schemas Makefile | head -n 80\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260711-002-r12s1\ntitle: \"Overlap stalled stores with a posted write buffer\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The pipeline currently freezes from MEM back through fetch whenever a store sees\n  dmemReady low. In the fitness workload the data bus is randomly stalled about 22%\n  of cycles, yet a store has no result needed by younger arithmetic instructions.\n  This leaves useful execute bandwidth idle and makes store backpressure more costly\n  than its architectural ordering requires.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a one-entry posted-store buffer at the memory stage. A store that cannot\n  handshake immediately will copy its address, replicated data, and byte mask into\n  the buffer and advance to retirement exactly once, allowing younger non-memory\n  instructions to continue while the buffered write drains. Any younger load or\n  store remains ordered behind the pending write and stalls until the buffer either\n  drains or can be replaced on the same edge; zero-wait stores retain the existing\n  direct path. Keeping the optimization off the ALU, fetch, and register-file paths\n  should preserve most of the present Fmax while converting a fraction of random\n  dmem stall cycles into useful execution. MMIO writes, reset, redirects, RVFI store\n  metadata, and exactly-once external write handshakes must retain current behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-entry posted-store register, direct zero-wait bypass, buffered dmem driving, same-cycle drain/refill handling, and status signals that preserve exactly-once store retirement and bus writes.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace unconditional store backpressure with memory-order blocking: loads and later stores wait behind a pending write, while non-memory instructions continue and ordinary load stalls remain unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/zcore.sv\n    description: \"Wire store-buffer occupancy, drain, and memory-stage blocking through the existing nret=1 pipeline without changing the top-level interface or RVFI ordering.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed and randomized tests for stalled-store posting, independent ALU overlap, ordered load/store followers, same-cycle drain/refill, MMIO writes, reset, and exactly-once RVFI and external-memory effects.\"\ntools/tournament.py:54:# The hypothesis schema's `category` enum, in the order the brief specifies.\ntools/tournament.py:218:    import jsonschema\ntools/tournament.py:262:    except (jsonschema.ValidationError, FileNotFoundError, yaml.YAMLError) as e:\ntools/agents/static_agent.py:94:        \"      No-op placeholder to satisfy the hypothesis schema's\\n\"\ntools/agents/implement.py:170:        hypothesis = yaml.safe_load(f)\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:161:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:185:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:218:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:235:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/test_core_yaml_update.py:24:    y = yaml.safe_load((core_dir / \"core.yaml\").read_text())\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:282:## Required YAML structure (validates against schemas/hypothesis.schema.json)\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:338:        data = yaml.safe_load(raw)\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:351:            data = yaml.safe_load(repaired)\ntools/eval/formal.py:32:    y = yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()) or {}\ntools/orchestrator.py:6:import jsonschema, yaml\ntools/orchestrator.py:48:HYP_SCHEMA     = json.loads(Path(\"schemas/hypothesis.schema.json