{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r1s1.yaml; ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; require \\\"json\\\"; p YAML.safe_load_file(ARGV[0])' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r1s1.yaml >/dev/null && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r1s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260711-002-r1s1\ntitle: \"Replace combinational division with an iterative M-unit\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The post-route critical path runs from ID/EX through the synthesized divide/remainder cone into EX/MEM, reaching roughly 7.9 ns and limiting the median Fmax to 127.03 MHz. The same combinational divider also contributes substantial LUT and routing pressure in a design already using 9563 LUT4s, whereas the CoreMark binary contains only a handful of static DIVU sites.\nhypothesis: |\n  Move DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU out of the combinational ALU into a shared radix-2 iterative divider. On a divide instruction, capture the forwarded operands and instruction metadata, freeze the younger pipeline and EX/MEM advancement while the unit iterates, then inject the architecturally correct quotient or remainder into EX/MEM exactly once when done. Keep ordinary ALU and DSP-backed multiply instructions single-cycle. Removing the unrolled divider cone should materially raise Fmax and reduce placement congestion; the low dynamic division frequency should make the added divide latency much smaller than the clock-rate gain. Preserve divide-by-zero and signed-overflow semantics, RVFI operands/order, bus-stall priority, redirects, and the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 15\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/div_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a shared iterative signed/unsigned quotient-remainder unit with start, busy, done, and result handshaking plus all RV32M corner-case semantics.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove real combinational divide and remainder operators from the normal hardware datapath while retaining the ALTOPS formal substitutions and single-cycle non-divide operations.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Recognize divide-class operations, capture their forwarded operands and pipeline payload, wait for the iterative result, and emit one completed EX/MEM transaction without duplicate redirects or retirement.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add multi-cycle execute interlocking that freezes IF and ID, prevents EX/MEM overwrite, and composes correctly with instruction/data bus stalls and redirect flushing.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the divider busy/completion handshake through execute and hazard control while preserving the nret=1 top-level and RVFI interface.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Adapt unit coverage so combinational ALU tests continue to cover non-divide and ALTOPS behavior while division correctness is exercised through the multi-cycle path.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add pipeline tests for dependent and back-to-back DIV/REM operations, corner cases, random imem/dmem stalls, and exactly-once RVFI retirement during execute interlocks.\"\n-e:1:in `<main>': undefined method `safe_load_file' for Psych:Module (NoMethodError)\nDid you mean?  safe_load\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
