rough execute and hazard control while preserving the nret=1 top-level and RVFI interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Adapt unit coverage so combinational ALU tests continue to cover non-divide and ALTOPS behavior while division correctness is exercised through the multi-cycle path.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add pipeline tests for dependent and back-to-back DIV/REM operations, corner cases, random imem/dmem stalls, and exactly-once RVFI retirement during execute interlocks.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 15, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/div_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a shared iterative signed/unsigned quotient-remainder unit with start, busy, done, and result handshaking plus all RV32M corner-case semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational divide and remainder operators from the normal hardware datapath while retaining the ALTOPS formal substitutions and single-cycle non-divide operations.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize divide-class operations, capture their forwarded operands and pipeline payload, wait for the iterative result, and emit one completed EX/MEM transaction without duplicate redirects or retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add multi-cycle execute interlocking that freezes IF and ID, prevents EX/MEM overwrite, and composes correctly with instruction/data bus stalls and redirect flushing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the divider busy/completion handshake through execute and hazard control while preserving the nret=1 top-level and RVFI interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Adapt unit coverage so combinational ALU tests continue to cover non-divide and ALTOPS behavior while division correctness is exercised through the multi-cycle path.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.