{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r9s1.yaml; rg -n 'hypothesis.schema|jsonschema|yamllint|validate.*hypothesis' Makefile tools schemas | head -n 80; git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r9s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260711-002-r9s1\ntitle: \"Register multiply behind the execute interlock\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  After iterative division removed the dominant LUT cone, synthesis still maps the\n  multiply family to a 36-by-36 DSP whose result and operation-selection logic feed\n  the EX/MEM setup path combinationally. The current design already has a verified\n  multi-cycle execute interlock, while the failed 33-bit sharing experiment showed\n  that operand muxing before a combinational multiplier is especially costly.\nhypothesis: |\n  Move MUL, MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU out of the combinational ALU into a dedicated\n  registered multiply unit. Capture the already-forwarded native 32-bit operands\n  and operation, perform the signedness-specific product behind a register boundary,\n  and inject the selected result into EX/MEM exactly once on the following cycle.\n  Reuse the divider's execute hold and completion discipline so ordinary RV32I ALU,\n  branch, load, and store instructions retain their existing latency and datapaths.\n  This should let the FPGA mapper use the DSP's registered path and remove the wide\n  product cone from the normal EX critical path; the one-cycle penalty only on\n  multiply instructions should be smaller than the resulting Fmax gain. Preserve\n  the combinational RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions, exact RV32M signedness,\n  forwarded RVFI operands, bus-stall priority, and exactly-once retirement.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/mul_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a registered native-width RV32M multiplier with start/done/accept handshaking and exact low/high signedness selection, structured for DSP input/output register inference.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove real multiply products from the ordinary combinational hardware datapath while retaining every RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS multiply substitution unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Dispatch multiply-class operations to the registered unit, retain captured forwarded operands for RVFI, and emit one EX/MEM transaction when the product completes without disturbing divider behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Generalize the existing multi-cycle execute wait interlock to cover multiply completion while preserving redirect and imem/dmem backpressure priorities.\"\n  - file: rtl/zcore.sv\n    description: \"Wire the generalized execute wait signal through the nret=1 pipeline without changing the top-level IO or retirement contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Keep unit coverage for ALTOPS substitutions and move real MUL-family result expectations to the registered execution path where appropriate.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add dependent, back-to-back, and signed high-half multiply cases under randomized bus stalls, checking exact results, RVFI operands, and exactly-once ordered retirement.\"\ntools/agents/static_agent.py:94:        \"      No-op placeholder to satisfy the hypothesis schema's\\n\"\ntools/orchestrator.py:6:import jsonschema, yaml\ntools/orchestrator.py:48:HYP_SCHEMA     = json.loads(Path(\"schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\").read_text())\ntools/orchestrator.py:444:def validate_hypothesis(hyp_path: str) -> dict:\ntools/orchestrator.py:447:    jsonschema.validate(hyp, HYP_SCHEMA)\ntools/tournament.py:54:# The hypothesis schema's `category` enum, in the order the brief specifies.\ntools/tournament.py:218:    import jsonschema\ntools/tournament.py:220:        emit_verilog, offlim