and carry one predicted marker with the instruction. EX compares\n  the resolved architectural next PC with the implied fixed target and gives\n  recovery unconditional priority, selecting redirect_target for loop exit,\n  signature mismatch, arbitrary instruction contents, traps, and aliases. This\n  should retain the measured hot-loop cycle benefit while limiting the live PC\n  path addition to a registered bit and a narrow constant-addend selection.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a single predicted-hot-backedge marker to IF/ID and ID/EX without carrying a target or predicted PC.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Implement exact preceding-PC lookahead, cancellation on stalls or discontinuities, and an addend-select PC update that reuses the existing incrementer; EX redirect_target must have highest priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the one-bit prediction marker with the instruction and clear it on every existing flush or bubble path.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Validate the fixed prediction against the resolved architectural next PC and issue exact recovery for not-taken exits, aliases, non-control instructions, target mismatch, or traps.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Route only prediction recovery through the existing redirect flush behavior while preserving all load, divide, and bus-backpressure interlocks.\"\n  - file: rtl/zcore.sv\n    description: \"Connect the prediction marker and exact EX recovery path without changing the nret=1 top-level or RVFI retirement contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Test correct hot-backedge prediction, loop exit, fixed-PC non-branch aliases, redirect priority, and randomized imem/dmem stalls with ordered RVFI retirement.\"\n-e:1:in `<main>': undefined method `safe_load_file' for Psych:Module (NoMethodError)\nDid you mean? 