{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260711-003-r8s2\\\") | {hypothesis:.hypothesis, fitness, delta_pct, fmax_mhz, cycles, implementation_notes, lesson}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260711-003-r8s2\\\") | {hypothesis:.hypothesis, fitness, delta_pct, fmax_mhz, cycles, implementation_notes, lesson}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The one-entry loop predictor reduced CoreMark cycles by about four percent, but\\nevery prior predictor placed a tag comparison or instruction decode directly on\\nthe fetch-to-PC path and lost much more Fmax than it gained in IPC. The sequential\\nfetch stream exposes the next word address one cycle early, allowing a loop-entry\\nlookup to finish in a register before the candidate branch reaches fetch.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Add a single-entry last-taken conditional-branch predictor whose full-PC tag is\\ncompared against pc+4 during the preceding sequential fetch cycle. Register the\\nlookup hit and cached target, then apply that registered result only if the next\\ncycle actually fetches the looked-ahead PC; redirects, stalls, or discontinuities\\ncancel it. Thus the full tag comparison and predictor-state read terminate at\\nflops instead of entering the PC critical path, while only an already-registered\\nhit and target use the existing PC redirect selection. Carry one predicted-taken\\nbit with the branch, train on resolved taken conditional branches, invalidate a\\nmatching entry on not-taken resolution, and recover in EX on direction mismatch.\\nThis should retain part of the measured hot-loop cycle reduction with materially\\nless Fmax damage than combinational, compressed, or multi-entry BTB attempts.\\n\",\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"fitness_delta_pct\": 2,\n      \"confidence\": \"low\"\n    },\n    \"changes\": [\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Add a one-bit predicted-taken marker to IF/ID and ID/EX; no predicted target is carried through the pipeline.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Implement the single-entry branch PC/target state, a registered pc+4 lookahead lookup, exact lookup-PC alignment checks, and cancellation on stalls or redirects before using the registered prediction.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Latch the aligned predicted-taken marker with the fetched instruction and clear it through existing flush handling.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Emit conditional-branch training information and recover only when actual direction differs from the carried prediction, preserving target-misalignment traps and RVFI pc_wdata.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Treat predictor recovery as the existing redirect and flush event without changing load-use, divide, or bus-backpressure interlocks.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/zcore.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Connect registered predictor lookup, EX training, and recovery while preserving the nret=1 top-level and retirement interface.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n        \"description\": \"Test predictor warm-up and taken hits, loop exit recovery, lookup cancellation across imem stalls and redirects, alias misses, misaligned targets, and ordered RVFI retirement.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"fitness\": 192.87,\n  \"delta_pct\": -56.28,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 85.01,\n  \"cycles\": 4407554,\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n  \"lesson\": null\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The selected angle is a one-entry branch-folding buffer: after a taken target has been observed, replay its cached first instruction on later exact target hits and redirect fetch to target+4. It avoids speculative fetch-PC lookup and only touches the already-taken redirect path."}}
