{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260711-003-r2s2\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260711-003-r6s2\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260711-003-r7s2\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260711-003-r8s2\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260711-003-r10s2\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260711-003-r11s2\\\")' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20260711-003-r2s2\",\"title\":\"Predict direct JAL targets in fetch\",\"category\":\"predictor\",\"motivation\":\"The pipeline currently treats every JAL as an EX-stage redirect, discarding the\\nalready fetched target instruction and paying a control bubble for direct calls\\nand unconditional jumps. A JAL target is encoded entirely in the fetched\\ninstruction, so it can be predicted exactly without a BTB, history table, or\\naliasing risk. The previous combined JAL and conditional-branch proposal failed\\nduring implementation compilation, making a narrower predictor the best path to\\nretain useful control-flow speedup with much lower RTL and timing risk.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The pipeline currently treats every JAL as an EX-stage redirect, discarding the\\nalready fetched target instruction and paying a control bubble for direct calls\\nand unconditional jumps. A JAL target is encoded entirely in the fetched\\ninstruction, so it can be predicted exactly without a BTB, history table, or\\naliasing risk. The previous combined JAL and conditional-branch proposal failed\\nduring implementation compilation, making a narrower predictor the best path to\\nretain useful control-flow speedup with much lower RTL and timing risk.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Decode only the JAL opcode and J-immediate in IF, select pc+imm as the predicted\\nnext fetch address, and carry that predicted next PC to EX. EX will compare the\\narchitecturally resolved next PC against the prediction and redirect/flush only\\non a mismatch, including recovery to pc+4 for a misaligned JAL trap. All other\\ninstructions remain predict-not-taken and preserve the existing recovery path.\\nThis stateless, always-correct prediction should remove the EX redirect penalty\\nfor every aligned direct call and jump while adding only a small immediate adder\\nand metadata register, so iterations per cycle should rise with little Fmax loss.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add predicted-next-PC metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Recognize fetched JAL instructions, form their J-immediate target, advance the PC to that target, and emit the selected predicted next PC while respecting stalls and recovery priority.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch predicted-next-PC metadata with the instruction into ID/EX.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Generate a recovery redirect only when resolved next PC differs from the carried prediction, including misaligned-JAL trap recovery, while keeping architectural RVFI pc_wdata unchanged.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire the EX recovery indication and target through the existing IF and hazard redirect paths without changing the nret=1 interface.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Add directed checks that aligned JAL reaches its target without a recovery bubble and that misaligned JAL traps, suppresses rd writeback, and recovers to pc+4 under bus stalls.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add predicted-next-PC metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Recognize fetched JAL instructions, form their J-immediate target, advance the PC to that target, and emit the selected predicted next PC while respecting stalls and recovery priority.\"},{