e\\nloop exit.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The baseline pays a redirect bubble for every taken conditional loop branch, but\\nall broader predictor attempts lost far more Fmax than their IPC gain because\\nthey added target arrays, counters, multi-entry selection, wide metadata, or\\nJALR/RAS routing. CoreMark's hot counted loops offer a much narrower opportunity:\\nthe same direct conditional branch and fixed target repeat many times before the\\nloop exit.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add a single-entry last-taken conditional-branch target buffer containing only a\\nvalid bit, the full branch PC, and its resolved target. A full-PC hit predicts the\\nbranch taken; a resolved taken conditional branch installs the entry, while a\\nresolved not-taken instance invalidates a matching entry. Restricting prediction\\nto direct conditional branches makes the cached target immutable for that PC, so\\nonly a one-bit predicted-taken marker must travel to EX. EX recovers on a cold\\ntaken branch or a predicted-taken loop exit and otherwise suppresses the existing\\nredirect. This should capture repeated loop backedges after one warm-up miss with\\nmuch less timing and placement cost than the failed multi-entry BTBs: there is no\\nindexed array, direction counter, unconditional-control decode, JALR path, or\\n32-bit predicted-next-PC pipeline payload.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":2,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add only a predicted-taken bit to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads, avoiding a wide predicted-target metadata path.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement the one-entry full-tag conditional loop target buffer, predict only on exact hits, and update or invalidate it from resolved conditional branches with recovery and bus-stall priority.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the one-bit prediction marker with its instruction and clear it on existing flush paths.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Train the entry from resolved conditional branches and generate recovery only when actual direction disagrees with the carried prediction, preserving misalignment traps and architectural pc_wdata.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Treat EX branch-prediction recovery as the existing redirect flush while preserving load, divide, and memory-backpressure priorities.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/zcore.sv\",\"description\":\"Connect conditional-branch training and misprediction recovery between EX and IF without changing the nret=1 top-level or RVFI retirement path.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Add repeated-loop warm-up, taken-hit, loop-exit invalidation, tag-miss, misaligned-target, and randomized bus-stall tests with exact ordered RVFI checks.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":2,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add only a predicted-taken bit to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads, avoiding a wide predicted-target metadata path.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement the one-entry full-tag conditional loop target buffer, predict only on exact hits, and update or invalidate it from resolved conditional branches with recovery and bus-stall priority.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the one-bit prediction marker with its instruction and clear it on existing flush paths.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Train the entry from resolved conditional branches and generate recovery only when actual direction disagrees with the carried prediction, preserving misalignment traps and architectural pc_wdata.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Treat EX branch-prediction recovery as the existing redirect flush while preserving load, divide, and memory-backpressure priorities.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/zcore.sv\",\"description\":\"Connect conditional-branch training and misprediction recovery between EX and IF without changing the nret=1 top-level or RVFI retirement path.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Add repeated-loop warm-up, taken-hit, loop-exit invalidation, tag-miss, misaligned-target, and randomized bus-stall tests with exact ordered RVFI checks.\"}],\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":360.87,\"delta_pct\":-18.19,\"vs_baseline\":27.6,\"fmax_mhz\":155.93,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"cycles\":4320996,\"iterations\":10,\"lut4\":5670,\"ff\":2129,\"seeds\":[182.62,149.75,155.93],\"formal_passed\":true,\"cosim_passed\":true,\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-07-11T22:03:30.810290Z\",\"slot\":2,\"round_id\":6}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260711-003-r7s2\",\"title\":\"Page-local compressed loop predictor\",\"category\":\"predictor\",\"motivation\":\"The prior one-entry conditional loop buffer reduced the measured CoreMark cycle\\ncount from 4.49 million to 4.32 million, but its full 32-bit tag comparison and\\nfull-width target selection cut Fmax enough to lose fitness. This shows that hot\\nloop prediction has useful IPC value, provided the predictor touches far fewer\\nPC bits and adds much less state and routing to the fetch path.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The prior one-entry conditional loop buffer reduced the measured CoreMark cycle\\ncount from 4.49 million to 4.32 million, but its full 32-bit tag comparison and\\nfull-width target selection cut Fmax enough to lose fitness. This shows that hot\\nloop prediction has useful IPC value, provided the predictor touches far fewer\\nPC bits and adds much less state and routing to the fetch path.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Replace the full-width loop-buffer concept with one page-local compressed entry:\\na valid bit, PC[11:2] tag, and 12 target-low bits. Train it only from resolved,\\ntaken conditional branches whose source and target share the same 4 KiB page;\\ninvalidate a matching entry when that branch resolves not taken. On a fetch hit,\\nform the predicted address as {pc[31:12], target_low}, so the upper 20 PC bits\\nbypass prediction entirely and synthesis needs only a 10-bit compare and a\\n12-bit target select rather than two full-width structures. Carry one predicted-\\ntaken bit to EX and use normal exact resolution to recover from loop exit,\\npartial-tag alias, page change, bus stall, or trap. This retains the measured\\nloop-cycle benefit of the last attempt while targeting a sufficiently small\\ntiming footprint to preserve the current high Fmax.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":3,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a one-bit predicted-taken field to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads, with no wide predicted target metadata.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement the one-entry 4 KiB-page-local predictor using a 10-bit word tag and 12-bit target low field, and preserve redirect and imem-stall priority.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the predicted-taken bit with the instruction and clear it through the existing flush behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Train only resolved same-page taken conditional branches, invalidate matching not-taken branches, and recover exactly when resolved direction disagrees with the carried prediction.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Use branch misprediction recovery as the existing redirect/flush event without changing load, divide, or bus-backpressure interlocks.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/zcore.sv\",\"description\":\"Connect compressed predictor training and exact recovery between EX and IF while preserving the nret=1 top-level and RVFI retirement contract.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Add same-page loop warm-up and exit tests plus cross-page exclusion, partial-tag alias recovery, misalignment, and randomized imem/dmem stall coverage.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":3,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a one-bit predicted-taken field to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads, with no wide predicted target metadata.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement the one-entry 4 KiB-page-local predictor using a 10-bit word tag and 12-bit target low field, and preserve redirect and imem-stall priority.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the predicted-taken bit with the instruction and clear it through the existing flush behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Train only resolved same-page taken conditional branches, invalidate matching not-taken branches, and recover exactly when resolved direction disagrees with the carried prediction.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Use branch misprediction recovery as the existing redirect/flush event without changing load, divide, or bus-backpressure interlocks.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/zcore.sv\",\"description\":\"Connect compressed predictor training and exact recovery between EX and IF while preserving the nret=1 top-level and RVFI retirement contract.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Add same-page loop warm-up and exit tests plus cross-page exclusion, partial-tag alias recovery, misalignment, and randomized imem/dmem stall coverage.\"}],\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":314.44,\"delta_pct\":-28.72,\"vs_baseline\":11.18,\"fmax_mhz\":135.87,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"cycles\":4320996,\"iterations\":10,\"lut4\":5523,\"ff\":2105,\"seeds\":[135.87,135.19,157.21],\"formal_passed\":true,\"cosim_passed\":true,\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-07-11T22:14:49.776284Z\",\"slot\":2,\"round_id\":7,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r7s2 (regression, -28.72%): Compressing a one-entry loop predictor to a 10-bit page-local tag and 12-bit target still leaves a compare and target mux on the fetch next-PC cone plus live-entry validation in EX, so CoreMark's saved loop bubbles cannot amortize even narrow combinational prediction unless lookup is staged or removed from timing-critical control paths.\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260711-003-r8s2\",\"title\":\"Registered lookahead loop predictor\",\"category\":\"predictor\",\"motivation\":\"The one-entry loop predictor reduced CoreMark cycles by about four percent, but\\nevery prior predictor placed a tag comparison or instruction decode directly on\\nthe fetch-to-PC path and lost much more Fmax than it gained in IPC. The sequential\\nfetch stream exposes the next word address one cycle early, allowing a loop-entry\\nlookup to finish in a register before the candidate branch reaches fetch.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The one-entry loop predictor reduced CoreMark cycles by about four percent, but\\nevery prior predictor placed a tag comparison or instruction decode directly on\\nthe fetch-to-PC path and lost much more Fmax than it gained in IPC. The sequential\\nfetch stream exposes the next word address one cycle early, allowing a loop-entry\\nlookup to finish in a register before the candidate branch reaches fetch.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add a single-entry last-taken conditional-branch predictor whose full-PC tag is\\ncompared against pc+4 during the preceding sequential fetch cycle. Register the\\nlookup hit and cached target, then apply that registered result only if the next\\ncycle actually fetches the looked-ahead PC; redirects, stalls, or discontinuities\\ncancel it. Thus the full tag comparison and predictor-state read terminate at\\nflops instead of entering the PC critical path, while only an already-registered\\nhit and target use the existing PC redirect selection. Carry one predicted-taken\\nbit with the branch, train on resolved taken conditional branches, invalidate a\\nmatching entry on not-taken resolution, and recover in EX on direction mismatch.\\nThis should retain part of the measured hot-loop cycle reduction with materially\\nless Fmax damage than combinational, compressed, or multi-entry BTB attempts.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":2,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a one-bit predicted-taken marker to IF/ID and ID/EX; no predicted target is carried through the pipeline.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement the single-entry branch PC/target state, a registered pc+4 lookahead lookup, exact lookup-PC alignment checks, and cancellation on stalls or redirects before using the registered prediction.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the aligned predicted-taken marker with the fetched instruction and clear it through existing flush handling.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Emit conditional-branch training information and recover only when actual direction differs from the carried prediction, preserving target-misalignment traps and RVFI pc_wdata.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Treat predictor recovery as the existing redirect and flush event without changing load-use, divide, or bus-backpressure interlocks.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/zcore.sv\",\"description\":\"Connect registered predictor lookup, EX training, and recovery while preserving the nret=1 top-level and retirement interface.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Test predictor warm-up and taken hits, loop exit recovery, lookup cancellation across imem stalls and redirects, alias misses, misaligned targets, and ordered RVFI retirement.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":2,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a one-bit predicted-taken marker to IF/ID and ID/EX; no predicted target is carried through the pipeline.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement the single-entry branch PC/target state, a registered pc+4 lookahead lookup, exact lookup-PC alignment checks, and cancellation on stalls or redirects before using the registered prediction.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the aligned predicted-taken marker with the fetched instruction and clear it through existing flush handling.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Emit conditional-branch training information and recover only when actual direction differs from the carried prediction, preserving target-misalignment traps and RVFI pc_wdata.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Treat predictor recovery as the existing redirect and flush event without changing load-use, divide, or bus-backpressure interlocks.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/zcore.sv\",\"description\":\"Connect registered predictor lookup, EX training, and recovery while preserving the nret=1 top-level and retirement interface.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Test predictor warm-up and taken hits, loop exit recovery, lookup cancellation across imem stalls and redirects, alias misses, misaligned targets, and ordered RVFI retirement.\"}],\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":192.87,\"delta_pct\":-56.28,\"vs_baseline\":-31.8,\"fmax_mhz\":85.01,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"cycles\":4407554,\"iterations\":10,\"lut4\":5554,\"ff\":2221,\"seeds\":[86.11,83.21,85.01],\"formal_passed\":true,\"cosim_passed\":true,\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-07-11T22:28:37.062159Z\",\"slot\":2,\"round_id\":8}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260711-003-r10s2\",\"title\":\"Lookahead addend-select hot-loop predictor\",\"category\":\"predictor\",\"motivation\":\"Prior one-entry loop predictors cut CoreMark cycles by about four percent, so\\npredicting a frequent taken backedge has demonstrated IPC value. Their fitness\\nlosses came from tag/decode logic and a separate full-width target mux on the\\nfetch-to-PC path. The fixed-image attempt also failed to prioritize the exact\\nEX recovery target, so it did not establish that a minimal fixed predictor is\\nunprofitable when recovery and the PC datapath are structured correctly.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"Prior one-entry loop predictors cut CoreMark cycles by about four percent, so\\npredicting a frequent taken backedge has demonstrated IPC value. Their fitness\\nlosses came from tag/decode logic and a separate full-width target mux on the\\nfetch-to-PC path. The fixed-image attempt also failed to prioritize the exact\\nEX recovery target, so it did not establish that a minimal fixed predictor is\\nunprofitable when recovery and the PC datapath are structured correctly.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Profile exactly one hottest conditional backedge, but recognize it one cycle\\nearly from the preceding sequential PC and register only a prediction-valid\\nbit. When that branch PC is reached, reuse the existing PC increment adder by\\nselecting its B-immediate constant as the addend instead of 4; do not add a\\ntarget adder, target register, predictor table, training path, or full-width\\ntarget-result mux. Cancel the lookahead on any stall, redirect, or nonsequential\\ntransition, and carry one predicted marker with the instruction. EX compares\\nthe resolved architectural next PC with the implied fixed target and gives\\nrecovery unconditional priority, selecting redirect_target for loop exit,\\nsignature mismatch, arbitrary instruction contents, traps, and aliases. This\\nshould retain the measured hot-loop cycle benefit while limiting the live PC\\npath addition to a registered bit and a narrow constant-addend selection.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":3,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a single predicted-hot-backedge marker to IF/ID and ID/EX without carrying a target or predicted PC.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement exact preceding-PC lookahead, cancellation on stalls or discontinuities, and an addend-select PC update that reuses the existing incrementer; EX redirect_target must have highest priority.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the one-bit prediction marker with the instruction and clear it on every existing flush or bubble path.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Validate the fixed prediction against the resolved architectural next PC and issue exact recovery for not-taken exits, aliases, non-control instructions, target mismatch, or traps.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Route only prediction recovery through the existing redirect flush behavior while preserving all load, divide, and bus-backpressure interlocks.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/zcore.sv\",\"description\":\"Connect the prediction marker and exact EX recovery path without changing the nret=1 top-level or RVFI retirement contract.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Test correct hot-backedge prediction, loop exit, fixed-PC non-branch aliases, redirect priority, and randomized imem/dmem stalls with ordered RVFI retirement.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":3,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a single predicted-hot-backedge marker to IF/ID and ID/EX without carrying a target or predicted PC.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement exact preceding-PC lookahead, cancellation on stalls or discontinuities, and an addend-select PC update that reuses the existing incrementer; EX redirect_target must have highest priority.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the one-bit prediction marker with the instruction and clear it on every existing flush or bubble path.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Validate the fixed prediction against the resolved architectural next PC and issue exact recovery for not-taken exits, aliases, non-control instructions, target mismatch, or traps.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Route only prediction recovery through the existing redirect flush behavior while preserving all load, divide, and bus-backpressure interlocks.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/zcore.sv\",\"description\":\"Connect the prediction marker and exact EX recovery path without changing the nret=1 top-level or RVFI retirement contract.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Test correct hot-backedge prediction, loop exit, fixed-PC non-branch aliases, redirect priority, and randomized imem/dmem stalls with ordered RVFI retirement.\"}],\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":403.44,\"delta_pct\":-8.54,\"vs_baseline\":42.65,\"fmax_mhz\":179.73,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"cycles\":4454888,\"iterations\":10,\"lut4\":5407,\"ff\":2057,\"seeds\":[189.68,179.73,170.91],\"formal_passed\":true,\"cosim_passed\":true,\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-07-12T00:20:52.932193Z\",\"slot\":2,\"round_id\":10,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r10s2 (regression, -8.54%): Reusing the fetch PC incrementer for a fixed backedge is not timing-free because selecting a 32-bit addend turns the constant PC+4 path into a muxed arithmetic cone, while the prediction marker and exact-signature recovery add cross-pipeline control cost that can outweigh one hot loop's saved bubbles.\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260711-003-r11s2\",\"title\":\"Resolved-target instruction folding buffer\",\"category\":\"predictor\",\"motivation\":\"Prior predictors saved several percent of CoreMark cycles but lost much more\\nFmax by placing lookup, target generation, or prediction selection on the\\nordinary fetch-to-PC path. Repeated taken loop branches still pay a redirect\\nbubble even though their target and the first target instruction have already\\nbeen observed, leaving an opportunity that need not speculate ahead of EX.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"Prior predictors saved several percent of CoreMark cycles but lost much more\\nFmax by placing lookup, target generation, or prediction selection on the\\nordinary fetch-to-PC path. Repeated taken loop branches still pay a redirect\\nbubble even though their target and the first target instruction have already\\nbeen observed, leaving an opportunity that need not speculate ahead of EX.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add a one-entry branch-folding buffer that learns the first instruction at a\\ntaken direct branch or JAL target. On a later resolved-taken control transfer,\\nrequire an exact cached source-PC and control-instruction match; on a hit,\\ninject the cached target instruction directly into ID/EX and redirect fetch to\\nthe cached target-plus-four address. On a miss, use the existing redirect and\\ncapture the target instruction when imem actually accepts it. This removes one\\nbubble from repeated taken backedges without predicting the branch direction,\\nadding a lookup to the sequential fetch-PC cone, or carrying prediction\\nmetadata through the pipeline. Restrict folding to direct controls, invalidate\\non replacement/reset, and qualify replay with all bus and pipeline holds so\\narbitrary programs, loop exits, traps, and exactly-once RVFI retirement retain\\nthe existing behavior.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":2,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/branch_fold_buffer.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a one-entry direct-control tag, cached target instruction, target-plus-four value, miss-fill handshake, and exact resolved-taken hit qualification.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Expose the resolved direct-control identity and taken target needed for exact fold lookup while preserving architectural redirect, misalignment-trap, divider, and RVFI behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Accept a fold-hit instruction payload with priority over redirect bubbling only when the pipeline can advance, recording the cached target PC and normal decoded/RVFI fields.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"On a qualified fold hit, use the cached target-plus-four as the existing resolved redirect destination; keep ordinary sequential fetch and redirect-miss paths unchanged.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Suppress the normal ID/EX redirect bubble only for an accepted fold injection, while retaining redirect priority and every load, divide, imem, and dmem backpressure rule.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/zcore.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire fold lookup, target fill, replay injection, and hit-qualified redirect selection without changing the nret=1 top-level or RVFI interface.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Test cold miss and fill, repeated taken loop hits, not-taken exits, changed control instructions, replacement, reset, and randomized imem/dmem stalls with exact ordered RVFI retirement.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":2,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/branch_fold_buffer.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a one-entry direct-control tag, cached target instruction, target-plus-four value, miss-fill handshake, and exact resolved-taken hit qualification.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Expose the resolved direct-control identity and taken target needed for exact fold lookup while preserving architectural redirect, misalignment-trap, divider, and RVFI behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Accept a fold-hit instruction payload with priority over redirect bubbling only when the pipeline can advance, recording the cached target PC and normal decoded/RVFI fields.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"On a qualified fold hit, use the cached target-plus-four as the existing resolved redirect destination; keep ordinary sequential fetch and redirect-miss paths unchanged.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Suppress the normal ID/EX redirect bubble only for an accepted fold injection, while retaining redirect priority and every load, divide, imem, and dmem backpressure rule.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/zcore.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire fold lookup, target fill, replay injection, and hit-qualified redirect selection without changing the nret=1 top-level or RVFI interface.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Test cold miss and fill, repeated taken loop hits, not-taken exits, changed control instructions, replacement, reset, and randomized imem/dmem stalls with exact ordered RVFI retirement.\"}],\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":283.83,\"delta_pct\":-35.66,\"vs_baseline\":0.36,\"fmax_mhz\":120.95,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"cycles\":4261344,\"iterations\":10,\"lut4\":5608,\"ff\":2288,\"seeds\":[116.08,120.95,126.33],\"formal_passed\":true,\"cosim_passed\":true,\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-07-12T00:40:28.219357Z\",\"slot\":2,\"round_id\":11,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r11s2 (regression, -35.66%): Resolved-target folding can still destroy Fmax without a fetch-side lookup because exact source-PC/instruction matching plus `fold_inject` creates an EX-to-ID/EX replay cone and selects target+4 on the redirect path, so branch folding needs a registered replay boundary rather than same-cycle decode injection.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
