6710, \"ff\": 2605, \"seeds\": [103.79, 108.45, 101.98], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T21:11:59.759048Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r3s2 (regression, -44.80%): Caching resolved targets does not make prediction timing-free: an asynchronous direct-mapped micro-BTB's tag compare, counter/unconditional decision, and 32-bit target mux on the fetch next-PC cone can overwhelm CoreMark's saved control bubbles, so BTB lookup must be staged or mapped to a timing-friendly memory structure.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
